@@ -1,5 +1,25 @@
 # deploy-demo
 
-Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main`.
+Deploys the service to AWS on every push to `main` and whenever a version tag
+matching `v*` (e.g. `v1.2.0`) is pushed. It can also be run manually via
+`workflow_dispatch`.
+
+## AWS authentication
+
+The workflow authenticates with GitHub OIDC; no long-lived AWS access keys are
+stored in this repository. It assumes
+`arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/deploy-widget` in `eu-north-1`.
+
+The role's trust policy must allow `token.actions.githubusercontent.com` as the
+OIDC provider (audience `sts.amazonaws.com`) and restrict the `sub` claim to
+this repository's `main` branch and `v*` tags, e.g.
+`repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/heads/main` and `repo:<owner>/<repo>:ref:refs/tags/v*`.
+
+The old `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` / `AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY` secrets are no longer used
+and should be deleted, and the old IAM user's keys revoked.
+
+## Secrets
+
+- `SLACK_WEBHOOK` – webhook used for deploy notifications.
 
 This repository is public.
